cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its recorded results, please cite it as below."
title: "olmoearth_inferenceX: label-free audit of Earth-observation prediction maps"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Qi
    given-names: Ziming
version: 1.3.1
date-released: 2026-09-25
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/2imi9/olmoearth_inferenceX"
url: "https://olmoearth-inferencex.readthedocs.io"
abstract: >-
  A Python package for assessing classification maps from Earth-observation models. Without reference
  labels, it ranks a map's windows by the model's confidence for manual review, lists the cues behind each
  flagged window, and compares two maps of the same area. With a labelled sample, it estimates the error rate
  and per-class accuracy with confidence intervals, and identifies the largest high-confidence part of the map
  whose error rate does not exceed a specified level at a stated confidence. The methods are evaluated on the
  24 tasks of Ai2's published embedding suite across 16 encoders; each recorded result is linked to a
  committed artifact and re-checked against it by the test suite.
